;; Datomic is the positional typed-data dialect over Protos Portion.
;; Text reaches Datomic only through Protos delineation; Datomic never scans
;; characters. A type's one Anatomy declares both Portion directions.

Kinds.[
  Datomic.{embody.[Result<Self Fault>] portion.[Portion]}
]

Types.[
  Fault.{Extent.Extent Problem.FaultProblem}
  FaultProblem.[Shape Head Value Arity MapPair Protos.ProtosFault]
  Boolean.[True False]
  Integer.SignedInteger
  Decimal.FiniteDecimal
  String.DatomicString
  Vector<T>.[T]
  Map<K V>.«K V»
  Option<T>.[None Some.T]
  Struct.{Fields.[Datomic]}
  Enum.[Unit HeadedUnit Payload.Datomic]
]

;; Canonical forms: True / False; finite f64 decimals with a point and no
;; exponent; None / Some.value; headless guillemet maps with alternating key
;; and value portions. Duplicate map keys fault at the second key. Comments
;; begin ;; and Protos drops them. Curly quotes are opaque, asymmetric and
;; balance-based with no escape. FiniteDecimal and DatomicString preserve only
;; representable Portions, so outbound printing is total and flat.
;; A head is a variant, re-emits itself, and may daisy-chain. In an expected
;; String position, one canonical Portion (including a.b, a!b, or a:b) is
;; recovered through Protos canonical text and may re-emit bare. Struct roots
;; begin {; enum roots begin at their selected variant. Parentheses land as
;; String until Meaning exists.
